{"tool_name":"marginalign","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"marginalign","home":"https://github.com/benedictpaten/marginAlign","license":"MIT","summary":"The marginAlign package can be used to align reads to a reference genome and call single nucleotide variations (SNVs). It is specifically tailored for Oxford Nanopore Reads.","addition_date":"2022-03-21T13:42:35.013596Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:10:45.884348Z","tool_type":["Library","Script"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:marginalign","credit":[{"email":"makeson@soe.ucsc.edu","name":"Mark Akeson","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"benedict@soe.ucsc.edu","name":"Benedict Paten","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer","Primary contact"],"url":"https://github.com/benedictpaten"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2977"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]},{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2977"},"format":[{"term":"FASTQ-like format (text)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2182"}]}],"note":"The Hidden Markov Model output is optional.","operation":[{"term":"Read mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3198"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1916"},"format":[{"term":"SAM","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2573"}]},{"data":{"term":"Hidden Markov model","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1364"},"format":[{"term":"Hidden Markov model format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2072"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1916"},"format":[{"term":"SAM","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2573"}]},{"data":{"term":"Sequence record","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0849"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence variations","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3498"},"format":[{"term":"VCF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3016"}]}]}],"name":"marginAlign","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/nmeth.3290","metadata":{"abstract":"Speed, single-base sensitivity and long read lengths make nanopores a promising technology for high-throughput sequencing. We evaluated and optimized the performance of the MinION nanopore sequencer using M13 genomic DNA and used expectation maximization to obtain robust maximum-likelihood estimates for insertion, deletion and substitution error rates (4.9%, 7.8% and 5.1%, respectively). Over 99% of high-quality 2D MinION reads mapped to the reference at a mean identity of 85%. We present a single-nucleotide-variant detection tool that uses maximum-likelihood parameter estimates and marginalization over many possible read alignments to achieve precision and recall of up to 99%. By pairing our high-confidence alignment strategy with long MinION reads, we resolved the copy number for a cancer-testis gene family (CT47) within an unresolved region of human chromosome Xq24.","authors":[{"name":"Akeson M."},{"name":"Fiddes I.T."},{"name":"Jain M."},{"name":"Miga K.H."},{"name":"Olsen H.E."},{"name":"Paten B."}],"citationCount":474,"date":"2015-03-31T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"Improved data analysis for the MinION nanopore sequencer"},"pmcid":"PMC4907500","pmid":"25686389","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"marginAlign","home":"https://bio.tools/marginalign","license":"MIT","summary":"The marginAlign package can be used to align reads to a reference genome and call single nucleotide variations (SNVs). It is specifically tailored for Oxford Nanopore Reads.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openeb